<div class="hwaet-project">
  <h3>Earthburn</h3>
  <p class="hwaet-project-meta">Short Film · Medieval Folk Horror · In Production</p>
  <p class="hwaet-project-description">
    A standalone short film adapted from the first act of the planned feature film, Drag Me to Winchester, following a medieval charcoal burner through a three-day charcoal burn in the New Forest towards his destined discovery of the dead body of King William Rufus.
  </p>
</div>

<div class="hwaet-project">
  <h3>Drag Me to Winchester</h3>
  <p class="hwaet-project-meta">Feature Film · Medieval Folk Horror · In Development</p>
  <p class="hwaet-project-description">
    Purkiss, a New Forest charcoal burner, charged with carrying the abandoned body of King William Rufus to Winchester, must make a two-day journey through a perilous landscape of ancient ghosts and Norman occupation - pursued all the way by the Devil himself.
  </p>
</div>

<div class="hwaet-project">
  <h3>Finding Folklore</h3>
  <p class="hwaet-project-meta">Podcast &amp; Film Series · Documentary / Folk Culture</p>
  <p class="hwaet-project-description">
    Storytelling, song and discussion exploring the myths, legends and living traditions of England. Series One released in 2024; Series Two in development.
  </p>
   <p class="hwaet-project-link">
    <a href="/findingfolklore/">View project →</a>
  </p>
</div>

<div class="hwaet-project">
  <h3>Unannounced HETV Project</h3>
  <p class="hwaet-project-meta">Television Series · 18th-Century Period Drama · In Development</p>
  <p class="hwaet-project-description">
    An eighteenth-century series set in the New Forest, based on the books of HWAET founder Brice Stratford.
  </p>
</div>

